    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issue 1: Governance Test - Missing Export\n**File**: `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n\nThe test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly, but it wasn't exported as a named export from the module. I added:\n```javascript\nexport { APPROVAL_STATUSES };\n```\n\n## Issue 2: Eval Test - Toxicity Metric Wrong Parameters\n**File**: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`\n\nThe `toxicityMetric` function was accepting `bannedTerms` as a second parameter, but `runEvaluations` was calling it with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs as toxic.\n\nI fixed this by:\n1. Removing the `bannedTerms` parameter from `toxicityMetric` - it now only accepts `outputs`\n2. Creating a `createToxicityMetric` factory function for cases where custom banned terms are needed\n3. Updating exports in `eval/index.js` to include the new factory function\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2705",
